536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'require >=1 attribute-read site outside the schema/config plumbing modules'","norm_id":"n9e9f27c8d52ee758","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A field is only read inside config.py's own re-export/passthrough code; if config.py is not in the excluded set the gate passes despite the field being inert","Implementer guesses a different plumbing boundary than intended, changing which fields fire"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"List the concrete excluded paths (e.g. src/rebar/**/_config_schema.py and the config loader module) in Scope, and state that reads anywhere else in src/rebar count.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the exact 'schema/config plumbing' files/paths excluded from read-site counting (e.g. _config_schema.py, config.py, _config_sources.py, _config_coercion.py) and state that a `.field` Load in ANY of them does NOT count — so the read-site boundary is deterministic and the 'no false fire on a live field' invariant holds even for uniquely-named fields whose only read is a config.py resolver.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["config.py:422 `return load_config().mcp.readonly` is the sole config-aware read of mcp.readonly and lives in the plumbing module config.py, which re-exports the whole schema (config.py:13-39) and defines load_config — unambiguously 'plumbing'","The soundness claim 'never a false fire on a live field' depends on which modules are treated as plumbing vs consumer, but no file/path list defines the boundary","A uniquely-named field (no cross-object terminal-name collision) read only through such a resolver would have zero counted reads once config.py is excluded"],"finding":"The 'schema/config plumbing modules' exclusion set — reads inside which do NOT count toward a field's read-site requirement — is never enumerated, yet it is load-bearing for the gate's soundness. For a UNIQUELY-named field whose only terminal-name Load lives inside an excluded config resolver (e.g. config.py's mcp_readonly()-style helpers that do `load_config().<section>.<field>`), excluding that module would make a genuinely-live field FALSE-FIRE as inert — contradicting the plan's 'never a false fire on a live field' guarantee. (mcp.readonly only escapes this because an unrelated `ctx.readonly` Load exists outside plumbing; a field without such a same-named collision would not.)","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8bc56415ce9eb118","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'require >=1 attribute-read site outside the schema/config plumbing modules'","norm_id":"ncbac51e23a07c094","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A new knob read exclusively via a config.py convenience resolver (like mcp_readonly()) but whose field name collides with nothing else in src/rebar — false-fires as inert despite being live","Implementer guesses a plumbing boundary different from intent, changing which fields fire (nondeterministic gate)"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"List the concrete excluded module paths in Scope, and note the specific risk: a uniquely-named field read only via a config.py resolver (the mcp_readonly() shape) must still be counted — either by not excluding config.py's read-through resolvers, or by requiring a read-via marker for such fields.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a brief doc/AGENTS.md (or gates-index) note describing the config-read DET gate and the '# read-via:' marker contract, or state explicitly that the self-teaching failure message is deemed sufficient.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'new check script (AST walk over src/rebar) + CI wiring'","Failing message 'teaches the escape and cites in-file examples' documents at failure time only","No mention of a gates doc / AGENTS.md entry describing the new '# read-via:' marker contract"],"finding":"The plan adds a new CI gate / pattern (config-read DET check with a '# read-via:' marker convention) but does not name where the new convention is documented for future field authors, beyond the runtime failure message.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd817f41c9d71bae","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n1fc4f09b5a657cb7","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A developer adding a new schema field with a legitimately indirect read discovers the marker convention only by tripping CI"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan specifies the read pattern literally as `cfg.<section>.<field>`, but actual read sites in src/ rarely start with a bare `cfg` name — they root at a call (`load_config().mcp.readonly`, `load_config().reconciler.max_acting_fraction`), a call on an arbitrary alias (`config.load_config(repo_root).verify.overlap_enabled`), or a section object bound to a local (`mcp_cfg.auth_introspection_endpoint`). The plan does not state the exact AST shape the check matches, and that shape is decisive: matching the literal 3-part chain FPs across most of the surface, while relaxing it invites the leaf-collision failure below.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f68cc739afeda9d5c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — \"require >=1 attribute-read site (cfg.<section>.<field>)\"","norm_id":"n47218bdf0dbc8f95","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Match on the `.<section>.<field>` attribute-chain tail (base-expression-agnostic) AND additionally recognize section-object-bound reads (`<local>.<field>` where `<local>` is annotated/assigned as the section type, e.g. `mcp_cfg: McpConfig`), rather than requiring a literal `cfg` root.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The read-site detection pattern 'cfg.<section>.<field>' assumes a fixed receiver identifier ('cfg'), but the plan does not state how the AST walk identifies a read when the config object is bound to a different name (self.config, settings, an aliased import, or passed as a parameter). An AST attribute-read match keyed only on the literal 'cfg' prefix would miss legitimate reads under other receiver names and FP-fire on genuinely-read fields.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda91ae881db7fa4d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'require >=1 attribute-read site (cfg.<section>.<field>)'","norm_id":"n5710b1a457011f15","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State the match rule: detect any attribute-access chain ending in `.<section>.<field>` for known section/field pairs, independent of the base identifier, OR enumerate the accepted config receiver names.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The `cfg.<section>.<field>` two-segment attribute-chain match will false-flag live, genuinely-read fields whose reads go through a bound section object or getattr, 